PATCH 614: initialize both 2ebe self-modifying far-JMP sentinels (board:0034).

Original 1000:2ebe-2ec8 sets DI=3ba6, calls [SS:0x31e], then sets DI=3bf1 and calls
it again. The target is 4cb9, which writes `ea <DI+5> <caller-CS>` at CS:DI.
Oracle writes 2082:3bf1 = `ea f6 3b 82 20` at 329.914 ms; port base-zero equivalent
is 0f69:3bf1 = `ea f6 3b 69 0f` at linear 0x13281. Ghidra dropped DI and caller CS
at both indirect calls, so the port left the second sentinel as raw image bytes and
patch 613's sound-node splice inherited a bogus link. The existing asm-backed 4cb9
implementation (patch 011) takes the two original inputs and writes both nodes.
Evidence: scratch/sequence-capture/snd-head/mem.watch.txt and FIST.DAT 0x12ebe.
--- a/fist.c
+++ b/fist.c
@@ -50130,2 +50130,2 @@
-  (*(code *)fist_icall_far((uint32_t)(DAT_1000_c31e)))();
-  (*(code *)fist_icall_far((uint32_t)(DAT_1000_c31e)))();
+  FUN_1000_4cb9((undefined1 *)0x3ba6,0x0f69);
+  FUN_1000_4cb9((undefined1 *)0x3bf1,0x0f69);
